---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "May 28, 2026";
const contactEmail = "info@blockprint.la";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms & Conditions — Blockprint"
  description="The terms that govern your use of the Blockprint website, the purchase of tickets, and your attendance at the festival."
>
  <article class="terms mx-auto max-w-2xl px-5 md:px-8 py-16 md:py-24">
    <!-- Wordmark links back to home -->
    <a
      href="/"
      class="block mb-12 md:mb-16"
      aria-label="Back to Blockprint home"
    >
      <img
        src="/brand/wordmark.png"
        alt="Blockprint"
        width="1010"
        height="152"
        class="w-full max-w-[360px] mx-auto"
      />
    </a>

    <header class="mb-10 md:mb-14 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl uppercase tracking-[0.3em] font-bold">
        Terms &amp; Conditions
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-xs md:text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.3em] opacity-60">
        Last updated · {lastUpdated}
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-content text-base leading-relaxed space-y-5">
      <p>
        Blockprint is a block party produced by Clavette Entertainment,
        LLC ("Blockprint," "we," "us," "our") on Abbot Kinney Boulevard
        in Venice, California. These Terms &amp; Conditions (the "Terms")
        govern your use of this website, your purchase of tickets, and
        your attendance at the event. By using the site, purchasing a
        ticket, or entering the event, you agree to be bound by these
        Terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the site or attend
        the event.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Use of this website
      </h2>
      <p>
        You may use this site for lawful, personal, non-commercial
        purposes only. You agree not to interfere with the site's
        operation, attempt to gain unauthorized access to any part of it,
        scrape or harvest data from it, or use it to transmit any
        unlawful, harmful, or misleading content. We may modify, suspend,
        or discontinue any part of the site at any time without notice.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Tickets and purchases
      </h2>
      <p>
        Tickets to Blockprint are sold and payments are processed through
        our authorized ticketing partner, Tixr. All ticket sales are
        subject to Tixr's own terms of service and purchase policies in
        addition to these Terms, and Tixr handles order fulfillment,
        payment processing, and any applicable refunds on our behalf. We
        are not responsible for tickets purchased from any source other
        than Tixr or another channel we have authorized in writing.
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>
          <strong>All sales are final.</strong> Except where required by
          law or as expressly stated in the "Cancellation, postponement,
          and refunds" section below, tickets are non-refundable and
          non-exchangeable.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Resale and transfer.</strong> Tickets may not be
          resold above face value, used for advertising, promotions,
          contests, or sweepstakes, or otherwise used for any commercial
          purpose without our prior written consent. We may void any
          ticket that we reasonably believe has been transferred or
          resold in violation of these Terms, without refund.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Valid ticket required.</strong> A valid, unaltered
          ticket is required for entry. Duplicate, counterfeit, damaged,
          or tampered tickets will not be honored. The first ticket
          scanned will be the one granted entry.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Pricing and errors.</strong> Prices, fees, and
          availability are subject to change. If a ticket is listed at an
          incorrect price due to a clear error, we reserve the right to
          cancel the order and refund the amount paid.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Entry conditions
      </h2>
      <p>
        Blockprint is a 21-and-over event. All attendees must present
        valid, unexpired government-issued photo identification showing
        date of birth at entry — a US driver's license or state ID, or a
        US or foreign passport. Admission is a revocable license, and we
        (and the venue) reserve the right to refuse entry to, or remove,
        any person at our discretion.
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>
          <strong>Search and screening.</strong> As a condition of entry,
          all persons and belongings are subject to search by security
          and law enforcement. Security may prohibit any item deemed
          harmful, dangerous, or not in the best interest of the event
          and its attendees. Refusal to be searched may result in denial
          of entry without refund.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Prohibited items.</strong> Weapons of any kind, illegal
          substances and drug paraphernalia, glass, cans, outside food
          and beverages (including alcohol), professional photo, video,
          or audio equipment, drones, laser pointers, air horns, and any
          other items identified as prohibited in our published event
          guidelines are not permitted and may be confiscated.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No re-entry.</strong> Blockprint is a no ins-and-outs
          event. Once you exit, you will not be readmitted.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Code of conduct
      </h2>
      <p>
        We are committed to a safe, welcoming environment. Disorderly,
        threatening, harassing, discriminatory, or unlawful behavior,
        failure to follow staff or venue instructions, or any conduct
        that endangers others is grounds for removal without refund and
        may be reported to law enforcement.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Lineup, schedule, and changes
      </h2>
      <p>
        Artists, set times, schedules, production elements, vendors,
        amenities, and all other aspects of the event are subject to
        change. The addition, substitution, or withdrawal of any artist,
        or any change to the schedule or programming, is not grounds for
        a refund.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Cancellation, postponement, and refunds
      </h2>
      <p>
        Blockprint takes place rain or shine. If the event is cancelled
        in its entirety and not rescheduled, the holder of a valid ticket
        purchased through an authorized channel will be eligible for a
        refund of the ticket's face value (excluding service, processing,
        and delivery fees, to the extent permitted by law). If the event
        is postponed or rescheduled, your ticket will generally be
        honored for the new date; refund eligibility, if any, will be
        communicated through our authorized ticketing partner. We are not
        responsible for travel, lodging, or any other costs you incur in
        connection with attending the event.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Assumption of risk and health &amp; safety
      </h2>
      <p>
        Attendance at any live event carries inherent risks, including
        exposure to loud noise, crowds, lighting effects, weather, and
        the risk of illness or injury. By attending, you voluntarily
        assume all such risks. You agree to comply with all venue rules
        and any health and safety measures we put in place. Do not attend
        if you are feeling unwell or have a condition that may be
        aggravated by event conditions.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Media release
      </h2>
      <p>
        By attending Blockprint, you acknowledge and agree that you may
        be photographed, filmed, or recorded, and you grant us and our
        partners the irrevocable, royalty-free right to use your image,
        likeness, and voice in any media, now or hereafter known, for
        promotional, marketing, archival, and commercial purposes,
        without further notice, compensation, or approval.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Intellectual property
      </h2>
      <p>
        The Blockprint name, logo, wordmark, and all content on this site
        — including text, graphics, images, and design — are owned by or
        licensed to Clavette Entertainment, LLC and are protected by
        intellectual-property laws. You may not copy, reproduce,
        distribute, or create derivative works from any part of the site
        without our prior written permission.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Disclaimers
      </h2>
      <p>
        This site and all information on it are provided "as is" and "as
        available," without warranties of any kind, whether express or
        implied, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for a
        particular purpose, and non-infringement. We do not warrant that
        the site will be uninterrupted, error-free, or free of harmful
        components, or that any information on it is accurate, complete,
        or current.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Limitation of liability
      </h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, Clavette Entertainment,
        LLC and its owners, employees, contractors, partners, and
        affiliates will not be liable for any indirect, incidental,
        special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for any loss of
        profits, data, or goodwill, arising out of or relating to your
        use of the site, your purchase of tickets, or your attendance at
        the event. To the extent any liability cannot be excluded, our
        total aggregate liability will not exceed the amount you paid for
        your ticket.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Indemnification
      </h2>
      <p>
        You agree to indemnify and hold harmless Clavette Entertainment,
        LLC and its owners, employees, contractors, partners, and
        affiliates from and against any claims, liabilities, damages,
        losses, and expenses (including reasonable legal fees) arising
        out of your breach of these Terms, your misuse of the site, or
        your conduct at the event.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Governing law and disputes
      </h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of California,
        without regard to its conflict-of-laws rules. Any dispute arising
        out of or relating to these Terms, the site, or the event will be
        subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the state and federal
        courts located in Los Angeles County, California, and you consent
        to personal jurisdiction in those courts.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Changes to these terms
      </h2>
      <p>
        We may update these Terms from time to time. When we do, we will
        revise the "Last updated" date at the top of this page. Your
        continued use of the site or attendance at the event after any
        change constitutes acceptance of the updated Terms.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl uppercase tracking-[0.2em] font-bold pt-6">
        Contact us
      </h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these Terms? Email us at <a
          href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}
          class="underline">{contactEmail}</a
        >. See also our <a href="/privacy-policy" class="underline"
          >Privacy Policy</a
        >.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm opacity-70 pt-4">
        Clavette Entertainment, LLC
      </p>
    </div>

    <footer class="mt-16 text-center">
      <a
        href="/"
        class="inline-block text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.4em] underline decoration-ink/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-ink"
      >
        ← Back
      </a>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* Anchor styling within the terms body — keep underlines but use the
     brand ink color and a comfortable underline offset for readability. */
  .prose-content a {
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
</style>
